---
import SubpageLayout from '@layouts/SubpageLayout.astro';

const _body = `<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="page-hero-inner">
      <span class="section-label">Truthful demo mode</span>
      <h1 class="t-h1">Live catalog data. Heuristic composition. Simulated execution.</h1>
      <p class="page-hero-sub">Your browser fetches the live Traverse capability catalog. A client-side name-and-namespace heuristic derives a plausible pipeline, then the page simulates its state changes. The composed pipeline above does not invoke published WASM, call an MCP endpoint, run the Traverse runtime, or use an LLM. You can also <a href="#discover-real">run one pinned, verified capability for real</a> — that opt-in path executes its published WASM in your browser and shows a receipt. See <a href="#discover-how-its-built">what is live, derived, simulated, and real</a>.</p>
      <div class="page-hero-badges">
        <span class="badge badge-accent badge-dot">Live registry data</span>
        <span class="badge">Derived by a client-side heuristic</span>
        <span class="badge">Execution states are simulated</span>
        <span id="discover-stats" class="badge">querying registry.traverse-framework.com…</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-sm" id="discover-root">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="discover-graph-panel card">
      <div id="discover-graph" class="discover-graph-el"></div>
      <div class="discover-legend" aria-label="Graph legend">
        <span class="discover-legend-row">
          <span class="discover-legend-title">Simulation</span>
          <span class="discover-legend-item"><span class="discover-legend-swatch is-idle"></span>Not used yet</span>
          <span class="discover-legend-item"><span class="discover-legend-swatch is-running"></span>Simulated active</span>
          <span class="discover-legend-item"><span class="discover-legend-swatch is-complete"></span>Simulated complete</span>
        </span>
        <span class="discover-legend-row">
          <span class="discover-legend-title">Line</span>
          <span class="discover-legend-item"><span class="discover-legend-line is-dashed"></span>Discovery</span>
          <span class="discover-legend-item"><span class="discover-legend-line is-solid"></span>Data flow</span>
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="discover-layout">
      <div class="terminal discover-terminal">
        <div class="terminal-header">
          <div class="code-dots"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
          <span class="terminal-title" id="discover-phase-title">live catalog · deriving a heuristic pipeline</span>
        </div>
        <div class="terminal-body discover-log" id="discover-log"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="discover-run-panel">
        <p class="t-body-sm t-muted"><strong>How to read it:</strong> the <strong>Goal</strong> is illustrative. The dashed line shows the page deriving an ordered pipeline from live catalog metadata; it is not agent discovery or an MCP exchange. The solid line shows the derived capability sequence and a <strong>simulated result</strong>. Click a capability to open its real published contract. The animation is only a visualization: it does not invoke WASM or execute a workflow.</p>
        <button id="discover-run" class="btn btn-primary" type="button">Discover another workflow →</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="discover-cards" id="discover-cards"></div>

    <div class="discover-real card" id="discover-real">
      <div class="discover-real-head">
        <div>
          <span class="section-label">Real execution · opt in</span>
          <h3 class="discover-real-title">Run one pinned capability for real</h3>
          <p class="t-body-sm t-muted discover-real-intro">This is the only part of this page that executes a governed Traverse capability. It runs <strong>one</strong> pinned, verified capability &mdash; <code>core/core.calculate-price@1.1.0</code> &mdash; <strong>client-side in your browser</strong> via <code>traverse-embedder-web</code>&rsquo;s BundleEmbedder: no sidecar, no network execution, no MCP loop, no LLM. The composed pipeline above stays derived and simulated; nothing here makes it real. If the artifact digest does not match the pinned value, or the host is unreachable, this fails closed &mdash; it never fabricates a success.</p>
        </div>
        <span class="discover-real-badge" id="discover-real-badge" data-state="idle">Real: not run yet</span>
      </div>
      <button id="discover-real-run" class="btn btn-primary" type="button">Run this one for real &rarr;</button>

      <div class="terminal discover-real-terminal">
        <div class="terminal-header">
          <div class="code-dots"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
          <span class="terminal-title">real execution &middot; governed browser host</span>
        </div>
        <div class="terminal-body discover-real-log" id="discover-real-log"></div>
      </div>

      <div class="discover-real-result" id="discover-real-result" data-outcome="idle" hidden>
        <dl class="discover-real-receipt">
          <div><dt>Pinned artifact / contract</dt><dd id="discover-real-identity">&mdash;</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Artifact digest</dt><dd class="discover-real-mono" id="discover-real-digest">&mdash;</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Contract validation</dt><dd id="discover-real-validation">&mdash;</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Terminal outcome</dt><dd id="discover-real-outcome">&mdash;</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Output hash</dt><dd class="discover-real-mono" id="discover-real-output-hash">&mdash;</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <div class="discover-real-quote" id="discover-real-quote"></div>
        <details class="discover-real-trace-wrap">
          <summary>Redacted per-invocation trace</summary>
          <pre class="discover-real-trace" id="discover-real-trace">No trace retained.</pre>
        </details>
      </div>

      <div class="discover-real-sub" id="discover-pipeline">
        <div class="discover-real-head">
          <div>
            <h4 class="discover-real-title">&hellip;or run a three-capability pipeline for real</h4>
            <p class="t-body-sm t-muted discover-real-intro">Executes <strong>three</strong> pinned published capabilities as one governed <code>direct</code>-triggered workflow &mdash; <code>period.finalize</code> &rarr; <code>summary.aggregate</code> &rarr; <code>uncertainty.score</code> &mdash; each node consuming the previous node&rsquo;s output, all real WASM in your browser, one execution event per node. <strong>The capabilities and their order are authored in the committed bundle</strong>, not discovered or selected at runtime; runtime discovery and capability selection are tracked upstream (traverse#1150) and are not part of this page yet.</p>
          </div>
          <span class="discover-real-badge" id="discover-pipeline-badge" data-state="idle">Real: not run yet</span>
        </div>
        <button id="discover-pipeline-run" class="btn btn-primary" type="button">Run the 3-capability pipeline &rarr;</button>

        <ol class="discover-pipeline-nodes" aria-label="Pipeline nodes">
          <li id="discover-pipeline-node-period_finalize" data-state="idle"><code>period.finalize@1.0.0</code></li>
          <li id="discover-pipeline-node-summary_aggregate" data-state="idle"><code>summary.aggregate@1.0.0</code></li>
          <li id="discover-pipeline-node-uncertainty_score" data-state="idle"><code>uncertainty.score@1.0.0</code></li>
        </ol>

        <div class="terminal discover-real-terminal">
          <div class="terminal-header">
            <div class="code-dots"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
            <span class="terminal-title">real pipeline execution &middot; governed browser host</span>
          </div>
          <div class="terminal-body discover-real-log" id="discover-pipeline-log"></div>
        </div>

        <div class="discover-real-result" id="discover-pipeline-result" data-outcome="idle" hidden>
          <dl class="discover-real-receipt">
            <div><dt>Pinned capabilities (in order)</dt><dd class="discover-real-mono" id="discover-pipeline-identity">&mdash;</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Terminal outcome</dt><dd id="discover-pipeline-outcome">&mdash;</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Workflow output hash</dt><dd class="discover-real-mono" id="discover-pipeline-output-hash">&mdash;</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <div class="discover-pipeline-outputs" id="discover-pipeline-outputs"></div>
          <details class="discover-real-trace-wrap">
            <summary>Redacted per-invocation trace</summary>
            <pre class="discover-real-trace" id="discover-pipeline-trace">No trace retained.</pre>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="discover-real-sub" id="discover-discovered">
        <div class="discover-real-head">
          <div>
            <span class="section-label">Runtime-discovered · opt in · discover → plan → review → execute</span>
            <h4 class="discover-real-title">&hellip;or discover, plan, and execute a workflow from a goal, at runtime</h4>
            <p class="t-body-sm t-muted discover-real-intro">This is the real target of the page. Your browser fetches the live <a href="https://registry.traverse-framework.com/catalog.json">catalog</a>, builds a <strong>digest-verified snapshot</strong>, prepares the exact WASM + contracts, and runs <code>traverse-embedder-web</code>&rsquo;s <strong>deterministic browser-local planner</strong> (Spec 1277) to derive a workflow from a stated goal &mdash; <strong>structurally</strong>, with no capability-name, namespace, natural-language, or model inference. The proposal is shown for review with every mapping <code>unconfirmed</code>. Confirming hands the reviewed proposal to the <strong>local governed runtime</strong>, which executes only exact, prepared, digest-verified <code>pure_read</code> components <strong>offline</strong> and returns a redacted per-node trace. It fails closed on drift, an unauthorized node, or a node error &mdash; it never fabricates a success. The browser is an untrusted proposer; the runtime is the sole authority.</p>
          </div>
          <span class="discover-real-badge" id="discover-disc-badge" data-state="idle">Discovered: not run yet</span>
        </div>
        <button id="discover-disc-run" class="btn btn-primary" type="button">Discover &amp; plan from the goal &rarr;</button>

        <div class="terminal discover-real-terminal">
          <div class="terminal-header">
            <div class="code-dots"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
            <span class="terminal-title">runtime-discovered planning &middot; governed browser planner</span>
          </div>
          <div class="terminal-body discover-real-log" id="discover-disc-log"></div>
        </div>

        <div class="discover-real-result" id="discover-disc-result" data-outcome="idle" hidden>
          <dl class="discover-real-receipt">
            <div><dt>Goal (structured target)</dt><dd class="discover-real-mono" id="discover-disc-target">&mdash;</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <div>
            <div class="discover-disc-sub-h">Derived capability chain</div>
            <ol class="discover-disc-chain" id="discover-disc-chain"></ol>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="discover-disc-sub-h">Field mappings (all unconfirmed)</div>
            <ul class="discover-disc-mappings" id="discover-disc-mappings"></ul>
          </div>
          <p class="discover-real-quote-note" id="discover-disc-note"></p>
          <button id="discover-disc-exec" class="btn btn-primary" type="button" hidden>Confirm mappings &amp; execute for real &rarr;</button>
          <div id="discover-disc-trace"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-sm" id="discover-how-its-built" style="background:var(--bg-elevated);border-top:1px solid var(--border);border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-label">How this is actually built</div>
      <h2>Four distinct modes, with one live source of truth.</h2>
      <p><strong>Live:</strong> this static Astro page fetches the public <a href="https://registry.traverse-framework.com/catalog.json">catalog.json</a> and links every card to its published registry contract. <strong>Derived:</strong> it groups current capability versions by namespace and orders a namespace with two or more active capabilities using a simple name-based verb heuristic (ingest → interpret → decide → act). <strong>Simulated:</strong> the graph animates <strong>idle → simulated active → simulated complete</strong>; it does not invoke a WASM artifact, MCP loop, runtime, or model. <strong>Real (opt in):</strong> the “Run this one for real” button executes a single pinned, digest-verified capability — <code>core/core.calculate-price@1.1.0</code> — as WASM in your browser via <code>traverse-embedder-web</code>, and shows the artifact identity, contract-validation result, terminal outcome, and a redacted trace. A second button runs a pinned <strong>three-capability</strong> pipeline (<code>period.finalize</code> → <code>summary.aggregate</code> → <code>uncertainty.score</code>) as one governed workflow, one real execution per node. Both fail closed on a digest mismatch or an unreachable host and never fabricate a success. In those two Real runs the capabilities and their order are <strong>authored in a committed bundle</strong>. <strong>Runtime-discovered (opt in):</strong> a third button fetches the live catalog, builds a digest-verified snapshot, and runs <code>traverse-embedder-web</code>&rsquo;s <strong>deterministic browser-local planner</strong> (Spec 1277) to derive a workflow from a stated goal <strong>structurally</strong> — no capability-name, namespace, natural-language, or model inference. The proposal is shown for review with every mapping <code>unconfirmed</code>; confirming hands it to the <strong>local governed runtime</strong>, which executes only exact, prepared, digest-verified <code>pure_read</code> components offline (over the <code>@1.1.0</code>, <code>is_automatic_eligible</code> releases) and returns a redacted per-node trace. The browser only proposes; the runtime authorizes and runs. The composed multi-node pipeline is not executed as a whole by any mode — the graph itself stays derived and simulated. Umbrella: <a href="https://github.com/traverse-framework/traverse/issues/1150">traverse#1150</a>.</p>
      <a href="/registry.html" class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm" style="margin-top:1rem">Browse the full registry →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>`;
---
<SubpageLayout
  title={"Live Workflow Composition Demo — Traverse Framework"}
  description={"Watch a client-side heuristic -- not a hosted AI model -- compose a real workflow from the live Traverse capability registry, right in your browser. No fixtures, no precomputed data."}
  canonical={"https://traverse-framework.com/discover.html"}
  crumbs={[{ label: "Home", href: "/" }]}
>
  <style is:global slot="head">
    .discover-graph-panel { position: relative; padding: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
    .discover-graph-el { width: 100%; height: 460px; }
    .discover-legend {
      position: absolute; z-index: 5; right: 1.25rem; bottom: 1.25rem;
      display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.35rem;
      padding: 0.5rem 0.7rem;
      background: var(--bg-elevated);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
      box-shadow: 0 4px 16px rgba(0,0,0,0.3);
      font-size: 0.7rem;
    }
    .discover-legend-row { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.7rem; }
    .discover-legend-title { text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; color: var(--fg-subtle); font-size: 0.62rem; width: 32px; flex-shrink: 0; }
    .discover-legend-item { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.35rem; color: var(--fg-muted); white-space: nowrap; }
    .discover-legend-swatch { width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 3px; border: 2px solid transparent; }
    .discover-legend-swatch.is-idle { border-color: var(--border); background: var(--bg-card); }
    .discover-legend-swatch.is-running { border-color: var(--accent); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 20%, transparent); }
    .discover-legend-swatch.is-complete { border-color: var(--success); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--success) 18%, transparent); }
    .discover-legend-line { width: 16px; height: 0; border-top: 2px solid var(--fg-muted); }
    .discover-legend-line.is-dashed { border-top-style: dashed; }
    .discover-legend-line.is-solid { border-top-style: solid; }
    @media (max-width: 520px) { .discover-legend { right: 0.6rem; bottom: 0.6rem; left: 0.6rem; align-items: center; } .discover-legend-row { flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; } }
    .discover-layout { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.3fr 1fr; gap: 1.25rem; align-items: stretch; }
    @media (max-width: 860px) { .discover-layout { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .discover-graph-el { height: 520px; } }
    .discover-terminal { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
    .discover-log { flex: 1; max-height: 320px; overflow-y: auto; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.4rem; }
    /* The terminal surface is a fixed dark editor background in both themes
       (matches .terminal / .code-block sitewide -- see components.css), so
       its text needs fixed colors too, not theme-reactive var()s that would
       flip to light-theme (dark-on-light) values and go unreadable here. */
    .discover-log-line { font-size: 0.78rem; color: #7d99a6; white-space: pre-wrap; word-break: break-word; }
    .discover-log-line.cmd { color: #f2ecdf; }
    .discover-log-line.ok { color: #9ccdb2; }
    .discover-log-line.err { color: #e8907d; }
    .discover-log-line.accent { color: #debeef; font-weight: 500; }
    .discover-run-panel { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem; justify-content: center; padding: 1.5rem; background: var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius); }
    .discover-cards { margin-top: 1.5rem; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr)); gap: 0.85rem; }
    .discover-card { text-decoration: none; display: block; }
    .discover-card-top { display: flex; gap: 0.4rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
    .discover-card-title { font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--fg); margin-bottom: 0.2rem; }
    .discover-card-id { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.72rem; color: var(--fg-subtle); margin-bottom: 0.6rem; }
    .discover-card-summary { line-height: 1.55; margin-bottom: 0.85rem; }
    .discover-card-link { font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--accent); font-family: var(--font-mono); }

    /* ---- Real execution (opt-in) ---- */
    .discover-real { margin-top: 1.75rem; padding: 1.5rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem; }
    .discover-real-head { display: flex; gap: 1rem; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; flex-wrap: wrap; }
    .discover-real-title { font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 650; margin: 0.35rem 0 0.5rem; }
    .discover-real-intro { max-width: 60ch; margin: 0; }
    .discover-real-badge {
      font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.72rem; white-space: nowrap;
      padding: 0.3rem 0.6rem; border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
      border: 1px solid var(--border); color: var(--fg-muted); background: var(--bg-card);
    }
    .discover-real-badge[data-state="running"] { border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--accent); }
    .discover-real-badge[data-state="ok"] { border-color: var(--success); color: var(--success); }
    .discover-real-badge[data-state="failed"] { border-color: #e8907d; color: #e8907d; }
    .discover-real-badge[data-state="unavailable"] { border-color: var(--fg-subtle); color: var(--fg-subtle); }
    #discover-real-run { align-self: flex-start; }
    .discover-real-terminal { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
    .discover-real-log { min-height: 3.5rem; max-height: 220px; overflow-y: auto; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.35rem; }
    .discover-real-log-line { font-size: 0.78rem; color: #7d99a6; white-space: pre-wrap; word-break: break-word; }
    .discover-real-log-line.cmd { color: #f2ecdf; }
    .discover-real-log-line.ok { color: #9ccdb2; }
    .discover-real-log-line.err { color: #e8907d; }
    .discover-real-result { border-top: 1px solid var(--border); padding-top: 1rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem; }
    .discover-real-receipt { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr)); gap: 0.75rem 1.25rem; margin: 0; }
    .discover-real-receipt dt { font-size: 0.68rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; color: var(--fg-subtle); margin-bottom: 0.2rem; }
    .discover-real-receipt dd { margin: 0; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--fg); }
    .discover-real-mono { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.72rem; word-break: break-all; }
    .discover-real-quote { background: var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius-sm); padding: 1rem 1.25rem; }
    .discover-real-quote-total { font-size: 1.6rem; font-weight: 700; font-family: var(--font-mono); color: var(--success); }
    .discover-real-quote-lines { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.25rem 1.5rem; margin: 0.6rem 0 0; }
    .discover-real-quote-lines div { display: flex; gap: 0.4rem; font-size: 0.8rem; }
    .discover-real-quote-lines dt { color: var(--fg-subtle); }
    .discover-real-quote-lines dd { margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-mono); }
    .discover-real-quote-note { font-size: 0.72rem; color: var(--fg-subtle); margin: 0.6rem 0 0; }
    .discover-real-trace-wrap { font-size: 0.78rem; }
    .discover-real-trace-wrap summary { cursor: pointer; color: var(--fg-muted); }
    .discover-real-trace { margin-top: 0.6rem; max-height: 220px; overflow: auto; font-size: 0.72rem; background: var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius-sm); padding: 0.75rem; white-space: pre-wrap; word-break: break-word; }
    .discover-real-sub { margin-top: 1.5rem; padding-top: 1.25rem; border-top: 1px dashed var(--border); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem; }
    .discover-real-sub .discover-real-title { font-size: 1rem; }
    .discover-disc-sub-h { font-size: 0.68rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; color: var(--fg-subtle); margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }
    .discover-disc-chain { list-style: none; margin: 0 0 0.5rem; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.35rem; }
    .discover-disc-chain li { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; font-size: 0.78rem; }
    .discover-disc-step { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.65rem; width: 1.15rem; height: 1.15rem; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; border-radius: 50%; border: 1px solid var(--border); flex-shrink: 0; }
    .discover-disc-digest { color: var(--fg-subtle); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.68rem; }
    .discover-disc-mappings { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.3rem; font-size: 0.75rem; }
    .discover-disc-mappings code { font-size: 0.72rem; }
    .discover-disc-unconfirmed { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 14%, transparent); color: var(--accent); }
    .discover-pipeline-nodes { list-style: none; counter-reset: pn; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem; }
    .discover-pipeline-nodes li { counter-increment: pn; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.45rem; font-size: 0.75rem; padding: 0.35rem 0.7rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius-sm); background: var(--bg-card); color: var(--fg-muted); }
    .discover-pipeline-nodes li::before { content: counter(pn); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.65rem; width: 1.15rem; height: 1.15rem; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; border-radius: 50%; border: 1px solid var(--border); }
    .discover-pipeline-nodes li[data-state="running"] { border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--accent); }
    .discover-pipeline-nodes li[data-state="running"]::before { border-color: var(--accent); }
    .discover-pipeline-nodes li[data-state="complete"] { border-color: var(--success); color: var(--success); }
    .discover-pipeline-nodes li[data-state="complete"]::before { border-color: var(--success); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--success) 18%, transparent); }
    .discover-pipeline-outputs { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr)); gap: 0.85rem; }
